<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Join Saline County History &amp; Heritage Society (SCHHS) for the 40th anniversary celebration on August 13th. Read more below.</p>
<hr />
<p><span style="font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 20px;"><script async src="https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com/pagead/js/adsbygoogle.js?client=ca-pub-9318701447515491" crossorigin="anonymous"></script></span><br />
<span style="font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 20px;"><!-- in articles - 2023 july --></span><br />
<ins class="adsbygoogle" style="display: block;" data-ad-client="ca-pub-9318701447515491" data-ad-slot="1423088530" data-ad-format="auto" data-full-width-responsive="true"></ins><br />
<span style="font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 20px;"><script>
     (adsbygoogle = window.adsbygoogle || []).push({});
</script></span></p>
<hr />
<p>Come to commemorate the inception of the SCHHS back in 1986 as a nonprofit – preserving, researching, and exploring the history and heritage of our Saline County community.</p>
<p>The fun is on Thursday, August 13. The program begins at<strong> 5:00 p.m.</strong> at 123 North Market St.</p>
<p>Show your support for history by attending this presentation, and bring a friend. There&#8217;s no charge to attend, and guests are welcome.</p>
<p>However, if you&#8217;d like to become a supporting member of the SCHHS, it&#8217;s $25 per year per household which helps to sustain our non-profit in educating the community on the county’s history, preservation of our great heritage, and providing a space for research.</p>
<hr />
<p>Browse MySaline&#8217;s list of all the events in Saline County at <a href="http://www.mysaline.com/events">www.mysaline.com/events</a>.</p>
